      "mappedStudentAnswerText": ": First we find position by Binary Search.\n① Start = 0, end = n-1\nmid = start + end/2\n② BinSech (int arr[], int x) {\nwhile (start <= end) {\nif (arr[mid] <= x) {\nif (arr[mid+1] >= x) {\nreturn mid;\n}\n}\nif (arr[mid] > x) {\nend = mid-1;\n} else {\nstart = mid+1;\n}\n}\n}\nWe got position, the value should be placed after arr[mid].\nNow, we make space by shifting values after mid.\n③ for (i = n; i > mid ; i--) {\narr[i] = arr[i-1];\n}\n④ Now, give value\narr[mid+1] = x;\nTime complexity O(log n) for binary search (worst case)."
